WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.800
Judge Judy Sheindlin is the most-watched TV
judge of all-time, known for her quips and

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.930
catchphrases, quick rulings, and no-nonsense
style …

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.180
"You bought the gun!"

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.140
"I understand that."

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.180
"You will pay for the damage!"

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.340
She's been on the air for more than 20 seasons
and counting, but there are plenty of behind-the-scenes

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.200
details even regular viewers don't know about
Judy and her TV court.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.360
Here are some facts about the outspoken judge
and her hit show you might not know.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:28.920
Judy makes bank

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.040
In exchange for her domination of daytime
TV, Sheindlin has been handsomely rewarded.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:39.040
According to the Washington Post, Sheindlin
renewed her contract through 2020 for an undisclosed

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:39.540
amount.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:45.600
But her previous contract netted her $47 million
per year, which she earned working only 52

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.340
total days out of the year, meaning she made
$900,000 per working day.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.229
That makes Sheindlin one of the highest paid,
if not the highest paid women in all of television

00:00:55.229 --> 00:00:57.940
— and she earns it largely by just being
herself ....

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:03.540
"Now, they pay me for doing exactly what I
was trying to repress for 15 years!"

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.040
Pre-show fame

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.440
Judge Judy went on the air in 1996.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:13.420
But in 1993, the Los Angeles Times did a story
on Sheindlin in which they referred to her

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.190
work in family court as a "highly personal
crusade to bring order out of chaos," which

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.360
"has assumed folkloric proportions in America's
largest juvenile justice system."

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.490
The story eventually led to a now-famous 60
Minutes profile, which in turn landed Sheindlin

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:32.200
a book deal, transitioning her from public
servant to celebrity author almost overnight.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:33.980
Judy's world record

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:40.030
In September of 2015, Judge Judy celebrated
its 20th season, which is a remarkable feat

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.350
for any TV show, let alone one that features
a cranky Brooklynite yelling at people for

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:44.980
20 minutes.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.480
"I want you to start banging your head on
the table and don't stop until I tell you."

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:54.380
But it was a landmark achievement nonetheless,
and one recognized by Guinness World Records,

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:58.380
who awarded Sheindlin that same year for having
the "longest career as a TV judge."

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.740
At the time of the award, Judge Judy had been
on the air for just under 19 years, which

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.560
amounted to 4,500 episodes and "more than
9,000 cases" heard.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.020
As of the making of this video, Sheindlin
is still presiding over her TV courtroom,

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:17.660
and with Judge Joe Brown's 2013 cancellation
after 15 seasons, it's unlikely that another

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.180
TV judge will ever even come close to her
record.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.060
How Byrd got big

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.380
There is no doubt that the success of Judge
Judy is largely due to Judy's powerhouse persona,

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.799
but the chemistry between Sheindlin and Bailiff
Petri Hawkins-Byrd is another crucial element

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.360
of the show.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.300
But it wasn't originally planned that way:
During an interview on Hollywood Today Live,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.640
Byrd revealed that producers had no idea he
and Sheindlin were going to banter, but it

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.280
happened in the very first episode ...

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:46.659
"She looks over to me and she goes 'S-O-D-D-I,'
and I just look and I go, 'Yeah, some other

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:47.240
dude done it."

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.920
Their comedy routine was born in that moment,
and Byrd says it changed him into a "principal

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.460
player" on the show and ultimately earned
him more money.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.000
But the crackling chemistry between Sheindlin
and Byrd didn't come out of nowhere.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:02.620
In fact, long before Sheindlin started doling
out her acid-tongued judgement for a national

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.540
audience, she was doing it in Manhattan Family
Court with Byrd right by her side.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.599
It was a tumultuous time in Byrd's life when
he got the unlikely opportunity to become

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.440
a TV star.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.520
He was working as a counselor at a high school
and delivering pizzas on the side to make

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:16.200
ends meet.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.860
Upon hearing about Judy getting her own show,
he wrote her a congratulatory letter, telling

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.720
her, "If you ever need a bailiff, I still
look good in uniform."

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.739
Amazingly, Sheindlin replied that they were,
in fact, looking for a bailiff, and the rest

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.480
is history.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.380
The curious clipboard

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:35.099
It's impressive enough that Bailiff Byrd basically
charmed his way into becoming an indispensable

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:39.640
character on one of the most successful daytime
TV shows of all time, but what he actually

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.440
does during filming elevates him to legend
status.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.620
Byrd revealed to Hollywood Today Live what's
really on that clipboard he's always holding:

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.580
crossword puzzles.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:52.459
Yep: While Sheindlin is busy hurling vicious
one-liners at the poor schlubs standing in

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.870
her TV courtroom, Byrd is getting paid to
play word games.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.180
Thanks for watching!

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.000
